Yes, that was true. So, this was a long game, and somewhat
interesting. My dwarven Archaeologist was yet another lurker, which
tried her luck, but actually first one to accomplish something. Now i
know most of the nethack tricks it's the early game which is always
much more interesting. Once a character gets to Gehennom it starts to
be pretty much boring. This character accomplished his task due to
certain strategy: being a dwarf allowed her to go for gnomish mines
first. Deep in gnomish mines she tamed 3 cats, and found a polymorph
trap. A while and a magic whistle later she had powerful companions:
balrog, vampire and yellow dragon. With those friends she stormed
dungeon with bravery. And on level 22 there was a bone file, which
helped her get most of remaining items for ascension kit and 6 (!)
artifacts. Staff of Misspelling evaded her grasp (she was lawful back
then), but the rest was stashed in her BoH. However, she never get a
proper weapon and skills and relied mostly on speed and pets. In
Gehennom she used unenchanted silver saber mostly, later changed that
for unenchanted Frost Brand. Because of powerful pets she didn't have
much respect for her opponents, and lost life twice. First time on
Medusa, while riding her dragon over water, lost her companion due
some nasty attack and got deep into the water (most of her spellbooks
drowned as well, and she never le-learned those spells back). Second
time in a tower, when kraken drowned her, and this time she lost most
of scrolls... This burned all 2 generated AoLS. She had an idea of
ascending with style, riding on a dragon, and even retrieved her
saddle with AoMB, but stashed saddle was eaten by some hungry monster
in the mean time, and no other saddle could be find :-(  Also, she
changed to male after mistakenly putting on wrong amulet after first
disaster.
Finding and keeping amulet was a tedious task, but he managed to do
that. Mysterious force this time was taking him back many, many times,
traveling upstairs felt like forever, and Wizard appeared several
times double-troubling twice. On planes however it was fast and
uneventful like never. End game took him no more than 2 or 3 minutes.
First altair was chaotic, but hey, there was this funny helmet in his
BoH..

rekrutacja, chaotic male dwarven Archeologist

